# Python analysis

## Conventions

- Match existing patterns in `utils/py/miniramses.py`, `utils/py/map2img.py`, and harness scripts (`plot_ot.py`, `plot_dmo_cpu_gpu.py`, `compare_dmo_outputs.py`, `check_ot_snapshot.py`).
- IC generators live under `utils/py/grafic/` (import sibling `grafic.py` from that directory).
- Prefer small, scriptable validation over ad-hoc notebook-style code.

## Validation

- Assert physical invariants (non-zero `emag` for MHD OT, density bounds), not just file existence — see playbook #5.
- When comparing CPU vs GPU, point to harness compare scripts and parity tolerances.

## Paths

- Do not hardcode cluster-only paths without noting `MINIRAM` / harness overrides.
- Keep plot outputs and scratch paths separate from repo commits.
